{
  "source": "Remediation profiles. CIS references are the CIS Microsoft Windows 11 Enterprise Benchmark v3.0.0 rule numbers, levels and values, taken from the MIT-licensed ansible-lockdown/Windows-11-CIS role; Essential Eight references quote the requirement and maturity level of $script:E8Requirements (lib\\Checks.ps1). Tiers nest: essential < recommended < strict. Debloat (the preinstalled apps of $script:BloatwareApps) is added by Strict or by -RemediationDebloat.",
  "tiers": {
    "essential": "Essential: the safe fixes of the findings, plus CIS Level 1 and Essential Eight Maturity Level One settings that are safe on any machine.",
    "recommended": "Recommended: Essential, plus the rest of CIS Level 1 that fits a managed machine and Essential Eight Maturity Level Two (attack surface reduction rules in block mode).",
    "strict": "Strict: Recommended, plus CIS Level 2, Essential Eight Maturity Level Three and opinionated hardening (outbound firewall rules for download tools, scripts opened as text, Windows Script Host off), and the removal of preinstalled apps. Some of it cannot be undone by the rollback file."
  },
